<sharedSelectionEntryGroups /><sharedRules><rule id="f9bfc0e9-f673-5fac-aa39-c69d9ad02d8d" name="Keyword: Screen" hidden="false"><description>Enemy ships suffer −1 BS when targeting a friendly Capital Ship within 3″ of one or more friendly Frigates. Screen protects only Capital Ships, never the Frigate itself, and multiple instances never stack — the maximum is −1 BS.</description></rule><rule id="2a663b74-6991-5c08-be45-eb2d4437644f" name="Keyword: Scout" hidden="false"><description>A Destroyers may deploy up to 6″ ahead of its owner's normal deployment zone, obeying all other deployment restrictions and squadron coherency.</description></rule><rule id="3b2564b9-26b4-5366-a571-9ee8d68fedd7" name="Keyword: Destroyer Armour Penetration" hidden="false"><description>All weapons fired by a Destroyer use AP D in place of their normal AP characteristic, Macrobatteries and Torpedoes alike. Their Torpedo Tubes also use Reload (1).</description></rule><rule id="f0d467af-62bb-5dc0-b3d9-8ec45ce7619b" name="Keyword: Squadron" hidden="false"><description>Escorts, Destroyers and Frigates have the Squadron keyword. Each is taken singly and up to 3 may be grouped into one squadron, which acts as a single unit for movement, shooting and Fleet Orders. Every ship in a squadron counts individually toward the fleet's Line Ship total.</description></rule><rule id="96d59a42-2eda-5ebb-8619-9c7837fbff35" name="Power Spur" hidden="false"><description>A reinforced ramming prow, carried by the Cruiser, Grand Cruiser and Battleship alone. It is not fired: it resolves as part of a Ram (Section 4a) at Strength equal to this ship's Prow Armour Value, and adds Devastating (3) and Armourbane to that attack. One per ship, and it occupies one Prow mount.</description></rule></sharedRules><catalogueLinks><catalogueLink id="21d4a2b5-b61e-53be-afb2-6e57a7045908" name="Open Play" hidden="false" type="catalogue" targetId="a1c4f0e2-5d37-5b90-8f21-6cb3d9a41e70" importRootEntries="true" /></catalogueLinks></catalogue>